  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 221141\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM HST Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on Tropical\nStorm Odalys, located well west-southwest of the southern tip of\nBaja California, and on Hurricane Polo, located a few hundred miles\nsouth-southeast of Manzanillo, Mexico.\n\nSoutheast of the Hawaiian Islands (Former TD 15-E):\nThe remnants of Tropical Depression Fifteen-E, located several\nhundred miles southeast of the Hawaiian Islands, has produced an\nincrease in showers and thunderstorms over the last few hours. The\nenvironmental conditions are still expected to be conducive for\nfurther development, and a tropical depression is likely to form\nduring the next day or two while the system moves slowly\nwest-northwestward or northwestward. Interests in the Hawaiian\nIslands should continue to monitor the progress of this system.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...70 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Katz/Pasch\nNNNN",
